te-beatrice","eventId":"purgatorio-event-30-1","label":"Ancient love renewed","sentiment":"positive","strength":"moderate","description":"Dante is overwhelmed by ancient love when the veiled lady appears.","isActive":true,"sortKey":30.000114},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-relationship-state-4","relationshipId":"purgatorio-relationship-dante-matelda","eventId":"purgatorio-event-28-2","label":"Pilgrim and forest guide","sentiment":"positive","strength":"strong","description":"The lady of the forest receives Dante beside the stream and invites his questions.","isActive":true,"sortKey":28.000108},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-relationship-state-dante-virgil-The Crown of Freedom","relationshipId":"purgatorio-relationship-dante-virgil","eventId":"purgatorio-event-27-5","label":"A will made free","sentiment":"positive","strength":"bond","isActive":true,"description":"Virgil declares Dante’s will upright and releases him to follow it.","sortKey":27.000106},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-relationship-state-dante-virgil-Virgil Is Gone","relationshipId":"purgatorio-relationship-dante-virgil","eventId":"purgatorio-event-30-2","label":"The guide has departed","sentiment":"positive","strength":"bond","isActive":false,"description":"Dante turns for his guide and discovers the loss; his gratitude remains.","sortKey":30.000115},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-relationship-state-dante-beatrice-Beatrice Names the Failure","relationshipId":"purgatorio-relationship-dante-beatrice","eventId":"purgatorio-event-30-4","label":"Judge and penitent","sentiment":"neutral","strength":"strong","isActive":true,"description":"Beatrice confronts Dante’s diversion toward false goods and requires repentance.","sortKey":30.000117},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-relationship-state-dante-beatrice-The Griffin Reflected","relationshipId":"purgatorio-relationship-dante-beatrice","eventId":"purgatorio-event-31-3","label":"Sight restored through repentance","sentiment":"positive","strength":"bond","isActive":true,"description":"After confession and Lethe, Dante is led before Beatrice and she unveils.","sortKey":31.00012}],"plotThreads":[{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-thread-ascent","name":"The Ascent","description":"The travellers climb from the shore through successive disciplines toward restored freedom.","color":"#718a70","resolvedEventId":"purgatorio-event-33-4","tags":[]}],"motifs":[{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-motif-ascent","name":"Stairs, Gates, and Height","description":"Every new height requires a threshold, an angelic permission, or a changed capacity in the climber.","color":"#78816a","tags":[]},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-motif-speech","name":"Prayer, Song, and Testimony","description":"Souls teach through prayer, song, confession, history, and poetic recognition.","color":"#78816a","tags":[]},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-motif-purification","name":"Burden and Release","description":"The mountain joins inward change with bodily experience, making moral effort visible and felt.","color":"#78816a","tags":[]}],"loreCategories":[{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-lore-category-edition","name":"Edition","description":"Reader-facing context grounded in Dante’s poem and the Longfellow edition.","color":"#71806c","sortOrder":0},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-lore-category-journey","name":"Journey","description":"Reader-facing context grounded in Dante’s poem and the Longfellow edition.","color":"#71806c","sortOrder":1},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-lore-category-form","name":"Poetic form","description":"Reader-facing context grounded in Dante’s poem and the Longfellow edition.","color":"#71806c","sortOrder":2}],"lorePages":[{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-lore-source","categoryId":"purgatorio-lore-category-edition","title":"Text, translation, and rights","body":"This reading edition preserves all 33 cantos, 4,755 verse lines plus 8 lines of Longfellow’s English note on Arnaut’s speech, and 37,410 words from Project Gutenberg eBook #1002, Henry Wadsworth Longfellow’s English translation of Purgatorio. Dante died in 1321 and Longfellow in 1882; Project Gutenberg marks the edition public domain in the United States. Downloaded source SHA-256: a84c5036f67ad127f1f39d144215bf116afb842c6b5a6d9a9dcd6f6d94cfdb60.","visibleFromEventId":"purgatorio-event-1-1","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[]},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-lore-structure","categoryId":"purgatorio-lore-category-form","title":"Thirty-three cantos","body":"Purgatorio is the second canticle of the Divine Comedy and contains thirty-three cantos. Canto headings preserve Dante’s numbered structure; scene titles are reading aids paired with their passages.","visibleFromEventId":"purgatorio-event-1-1","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[]},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-lore-terza","categoryId":"purgatorio-lore-category-form","title":"Terza rima in translation","body":"Dante’s poem is built from interlocking tercets. Longfellow preserves the three-line grouping and much of its syntax in unrhymed English verse; every retained source line remains separately displayed.","visibleFromEventId":"purgatorio-event-1-1","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[]},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-lore-geography","categoryId":"purgatorio-lore-category-journey","title":"The mountain and its terraces","body":"The maps interpret an island mountain opposite Jerusalem: Ante-Purgatory below the gate, seven terraces ascending around it, and the earthly paradise at the summit. Their scale is editorial and serves the poem’s ordered movement.","visibleFromEventId":"purgatorio-event-3-1","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[]},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-lore-chronology","categoryId":"purgatorio-lore-category-journey","title":"The Easter ascent","body":"The ascent continues directly from Inferno during Easter 1300. The calendar counts four days from Easter Sunday in 1300. Dawn in Canto I, noon in IV, evening in VIII, the new mornings in IX and XIX, sunset and the next dawn in XXVII, and noon in XXXIII anchor an editorial hour scale. Times between these cues are interpolated estimates, not measured durations. Histories told by penitents remain speeches within the ascent rather than false simultaneous timelines.","visibleFromEventId":"purgatorio-event-1-1","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[]},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-lore-lucia","categoryId":"purgatorio-lore-category-journey","title":"The journey made in sleep","body":"Virgil reports that Lucia carried the sleeping Dante from the flowered valley to the gate. She departs before Dante wakes; her help reaches him first through his guide’s testimony.","visibleFromEventId":"purgatorio-event-9-2","tags":[],"coverImageId":"purgatorio-image-character-lucia","linkedEntityIds":[]},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-lore-art","categoryId":"purgatorio-lore-category-edition","title":"Illustration provenance","body":"The world, portraits, objects, places, and topographic maps are original OpenAI ImageGen illustrations made for this edition in a mature late-medieval illuminated and engraved relief-map language.","visibleFromEventId":"purgatorio-event-1-1","tags":[],"coverImageId":null,"linkedEntityIds":[]}],"knowledgeFacts":[{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-fact-mountain","title":"The mountain permits ascent only by day","description":"Sordello explains that desire and movement upward fail after sunset.","readerLearnsAtEventId":"purgatorio-event-7-2","originEventId":"purgatorio-event-7-2","tags":[]},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-fact-prayer","title":"Prayer can shorten the waiting of the penitent","description":"Virgil distinguishes a changed divine judgment from love fulfilling what justice requires.","readerLearnsAtEventId":"purgatorio-event-6-2","originEventId":"purgatorio-event-6-2","tags":[]},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-fact-letters","title":"Seven marks measure the ascent","description":"The porter cuts seven letters upon Dante’s brow before opening the gate.","readerLearnsAtEventId":"purgatorio-event-9-4","originEventId":"purgatorio-event-9-4","tags":[]},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-fact-earthquake","title":"The mountain trembles when a soul is free","description":"The released shade explains that the mountain’s joyful shaking marks a completed purification.","readerLearnsAtEventId":"purgatorio-event-21-1","originEventId":"purgatorio-event-21-1","tags":[]},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-fact-matelda","title":"The lady of the forest is Matelda","description":"Beatrice calls the forest guide Matilda at the paired waters; Matelda is the conventional Italian form of the name.","readerLearnsAtEventId":"purgatorio-event-33-3","originEventId":"purgatorio-event-33-3","tags":[]},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-fact-lucia","title":"Lucia carried Dante to the gate","description":"Virgil reports that Lucia carried the sleeping Dante from the valley and departed before he awoke.","readerLearnsAtEventId":"purgatorio-event-9-2","originEventId":"purgatorio-event-9-2","tags":[]}],"knowledgeReveals":[{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-knowledge-reveal-1","factId":"purgatorio-fact-mountain","characterId":"purgatorio-char-dante","eventId":"purgatorio-event-7-2","note":"Dante learns this through the directly narrated encounter or testimony."},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-knowledge-reveal-2","factId":"purgatorio-fact-prayer","characterId":"purgatorio-char-dante","eventId":"purgatorio-event-6-2","note":"Dante learns this through the directly narrated encounter or testimony."},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-knowledge-reveal-3","factId":"purgatorio-fact-letters","characterId":"purgatorio-char-dante","eventId":"purgatorio-event-9-4","note":"Dante learns this through the directly narrated encounter or testimony."},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-knowledge-reveal-4","factId":"purgatorio-fact-earthquake","characterId":"purgatorio-char-dante","eventId":"purgatorio-event-21-1","note":"Dante learns this through the directly narrated encounter or testimony."},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-knowledge-reveal-5","factId":"purgatorio-fact-matelda","characterId":"purgatorio-char-dante","eventId":"purgatorio-event-33-3","note":"Dante learns this through the directly narrated encounter or testimony."},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-knowledge-reveal-6","factId":"purgatorio-fact-lucia","characterId":"purgatorio-char-dante","eventId":"purgatorio-event-9-2","note":"Dante learns this through the directly narrated encounter or testimony."}],"factions":[{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-faction-pilgrims","name":"The Pilgrims","description":"Living and completed travellers climbing toward freedom.","color":"#74806b","tags":[],"coverImageId":null},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-faction-penitents","name":"The Penitent Souls","description":"Souls undergoing the mountain’s ordered disciplines.","color":"#74806b","tags":[],"coverImageId":null},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-faction-guardians","name":"Angelic Guardians","description":"Messengers who keep gates, remove marks, and direct each passage.","color":"#74806b","tags":[],"coverImageId":null},{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-faction-pageant","name":"The Summit Procession","description":"Symbolic figures moving beside Lethe in the earthly paradise.","color":"#74806b","tags":[],"coverImageId":null}],"factionMemberships":[{"worldId":"purgatorio-world","createdAt":1792281600000,"updatedAt":1792281600000,"id":"purgatorio-membership-1","factionId":"purgatorio-faction-pilgrims","characterId":"purgatorio-char-dante","role":"Traveller","startEventId":"purgatorio-event-1-1","endEventId":null,"notes":""},{"worldI